[[:db/retract 17592186120221 :question/answer-fields 17592186117487] {:db/id 17592186119826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca426087-2ced-544a-8fc8-80a74f2884ad" "question-1146c0df-94bc-5e1e-b7ad-b9815bc6197e" "question-bc81db7e-a314-5809-b5c5-608d6bc1d824" "question-e2f7b0c6-34b9-5cdd-a2c3-dccbfbacb488"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119827 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cf27c214-ec1e-55e8-948b-06e561f6f7e7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2f4d4cbd-f2d7-5e35-a92b-2f2fb49fe824" "question-dbddc051-609a-50f8-b7fd-7c6e4c6d692b" "question-e1761a52-f68d-5dfd-83a7-02fd5760a09e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119656 :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n![](images/5c/5cb83f5140e0f687997fea631f78bb9d5cf7d6cbeef52fe746f4abcba9230a1a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{0}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5} = t,\t\\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{0}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\dfrac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/19/1998dafc905e62617ac4c8f57285a0d75cf0ef8bddf1e59be7eeea9149485017.svg)\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\dfrac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5}, \\; y=2\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-999b5494-410f-5564-a5e2-d9dbe0ae34c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119639 :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points ![](images/aa/aa4328c3ce96a1b9871e71f5cc27e255e47d186fe5848ea0f7d43b324d41a2d6.svg) and ![](images/9a/9a6a4549ad0127d861d9a5c0a1ceff0b41b7c06b648a327779f31b325ea5800e.svg) Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector ![](images/e6/e6db167bc32b19da05d87b24e9b910b80d32a1ef9e5965ab4cb5217a1fac4730.svg) which is given by\n![](images/e1/e17614c58be91b6165e40be1c489685e14898756db2d6a41bf80b638e666fc51.svg)\n\nUsing the point ![](images/1a/1aaddf0d4be4d873ff6c0600b0b239e0565a05ca8daaff7ca92bd5c70bebcf03.svg) and the vector ![](images/e6/e6db167bc32b19da05d87b24e9b910b80d32a1ef9e5965ab4cb5217a1fac4730.svg), we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n![](images/8d/8df9f1471a16c7b99e55290a41fe97641d62cef3bf5ba0e57e7fe6c029e98807.svg)\nor equivalently\n![](images/9e/9e688c295265c270ba7e1f66fc13ceebe9f6385ea45000c6f42c204d3fb6ba50.svg)\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because ![](images/74/7435bec0e47e7cfafdcbdbf0763b77d55a16344504663512cbbcf8b75a50381f.svg) involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the ![](images/90/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg) component always maintains the constant value ![](images/ef/efcfb7a56c85727ded8a9d5c9bd75fd79ac0bc20ba202c2da6aaca3c4e3ba503.svg) For example, our two points ![](images/aa/aa4328c3ce96a1b9871e71f5cc27e255e47d186fe5848ea0f7d43b324d41a2d6.svg) and ![](images/de/dee63698dc962e270612a470eb5e1eb23ffcbd72c8f9d787bc7eb927ff05f1c6.svg) both have ![](images/90/9032cb23a878659e74b670d3779a8cd4793b28af921eab1a6b3f2041a815e03b.svg)-coordinates of ![](images/ef/efcfb7a56c85727ded8a9d5c9bd75fd79ac0bc20ba202c2da6aaca3c4e3ba503.svg)\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the ![](images/74/7435bec0e47e7cfafdcbdbf0763b77d55a16344504663512cbbcf8b75a50381f.svg) part and instead write ![](images/6b/6be447d259b9b63c2cdd7adc4107d7c96ed4df1730890fc1bb5ce7cd585b8ea6.svg) as follows:\n\n![](images/92/92f849bc9c2fc37e54e4ecf4901b06624536d835db97d31f94ab77573d6e401b.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca426087-2ced-544a-8fc8-80a74f2884ad" :question/id #uuid "ca426087-2ced-544a-8fc8-80a74f2884ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-127074" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z+8}{-6}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z-(-8)}{-6},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(0,3,-8)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨7,2,-6⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7t \\\\ y=3+2t \\\\ z=-8-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-acbe6b35-1062-5ba5-b134-eaeb97e4203f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-acbe6b35-1062-5ba5-b134-eaeb97e4203f" :answer-field/id #uuid "acbe6b35-1062-5ba5-b134-eaeb97e4203f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-898d0828-6322-5cc9-9782-a0f2a96d4581" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5885116-09bb-5d3d-8d90-739f213a2b36" "answer-9024db90-ca7f-5e93-98cf-00227482d43b" "answer-898d0828-6322-5cc9-9782-a0f2a96d4581" "answer-4c21e0bb-ee8c-5fa2-ad4c-8c70768e7b7f" "answer-9177928a-2741-51e3-86bf-5cb26316adc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5885116-09bb-5d3d-8d90-739f213a2b36" :answer/id #uuid "b5885116-09bb-5d3d-8d90-739f213a2b36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=5t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=-8+6t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9024db90-ca7f-5e93-98cf-00227482d43b" :answer/id #uuid "9024db90-ca7f-5e93-98cf-00227482d43b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7 \\\\ y=2+3t \\\\ z=-8-6t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-898d0828-6322-5cc9-9782-a0f2a96d4581" :answer/id #uuid "898d0828-6322-5cc9-9782-a0f2a96d4581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7t \\\\ y=3+2t \\\\ z=-8-6t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c21e0bb-ee8c-5fa2-ad4c-8c70768e7b7f" :answer/id #uuid "4c21e0bb-ee8c-5fa2-ad4c-8c70768e7b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=-6-8t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9177928a-2741-51e3-86bf-5cb26316adc9" :answer/id #uuid "9177928a-2741-51e3-86bf-5cb26316adc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1146c0df-94bc-5e1e-b7ad-b9815bc6197e" :question/id #uuid "1146c0df-94bc-5e1e-b7ad-b9815bc6197e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127071" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the canonical equation $\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z+3}{-7}.$ Find the vector equation of the line." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z-(-3)}{-7},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(7,2,-3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨3,4,-7⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a00f7c00-cf28-532d-ba2d-23cd87582c37"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a00f7c00-cf28-532d-ba2d-23cd87582c37" :answer-field/id #uuid "a00f7c00-cf28-532d-ba2d-23cd87582c37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-299601c1-c189-56c9-a263-8a4e23810703" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8393d971-684a-53d4-b181-6839d28c8304" "answer-7acfe4e3-373d-5d11-a879-57c9a43b56c0" "answer-299601c1-c189-56c9-a263-8a4e23810703" "answer-4aeef7c0-439a-5ccb-8d85-ceb73b3ed2da" "answer-38f146eb-7159-527b-9b0e-80360837fbdb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8393d971-684a-53d4-b181-6839d28c8304" :answer/id #uuid "8393d971-684a-53d4-b181-6839d28c8304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7acfe4e3-373d-5d11-a879-57c9a43b56c0" :answer/id #uuid "7acfe4e3-373d-5d11-a879-57c9a43b56c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-299601c1-c189-56c9-a263-8a4e23810703" :answer/id #uuid "299601c1-c189-56c9-a263-8a4e23810703" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4aeef7c0-439a-5ccb-8d85-ceb73b3ed2da" :answer/id #uuid "4aeef7c0-439a-5ccb-8d85-ceb73b3ed2da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38f146eb-7159-527b-9b0e-80360837fbdb" :answer/id #uuid "38f146eb-7159-527b-9b0e-80360837fbdb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc81db7e-a314-5809-b5c5-608d6bc1d824" :question/id #uuid "bc81db7e-a314-5809-b5c5-608d6bc1d824" :question/math-academy-id "q-127076" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-10}{-6}=\\frac{y+5}{3}=\\frac{z+7}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{-6}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{3}=\\frac{z-(-7)}{2},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(10,-5,-7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-6,3,2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10-6t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=-7+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0cb77e23-9c21-5d3c-a6f6-d6c088c776f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0cb77e23-9c21-5d3c-a6f6-d6c088c776f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cb77e23-9c21-5d3c-a6f6-d6c088c776f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2aa0077e-181b-5c87-b397-bf90c7b66f48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cbce69e5-b398-5143-8fee-8b1fc3bf565b" "answer-55d1767d-6142-57fd-84ac-0823297abb7b" "answer-3a1b04c5-6fb6-5d48-9648-cb591bb11169" "answer-2aa0077e-181b-5c87-b397-bf90c7b66f48" "answer-2ff9e3e1-5e91-5965-a734-3ac520d19c3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbce69e5-b398-5143-8fee-8b1fc3bf565b" :answer/id #uuid "cbce69e5-b398-5143-8fee-8b1fc3bf565b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+6t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=7-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55d1767d-6142-57fd-84ac-0823297abb7b" :answer/id #uuid "55d1767d-6142-57fd-84ac-0823297abb7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=10+6t \\\\ y=5+3t \\\\ z=7+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a1b04c5-6fb6-5d48-9648-cb591bb11169" :answer/id #uuid "3a1b04c5-6fb6-5d48-9648-cb591bb11169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=10-6t \\\\ y=-3+5t \\\\ z=-7+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aa0077e-181b-5c87-b397-bf90c7b66f48" :answer/id #uuid "2aa0077e-181b-5c87-b397-bf90c7b66f48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=10-6t \\\\ y=-5+3t \\\\ z=-7+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ff9e3e1-5e91-5965-a734-3ac520d19c3e" :answer/id #uuid "2ff9e3e1-5e91-5965-a734-3ac520d19c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2f7b0c6-34b9-5cdd-a2c3-dccbfbacb488" :question/id #uuid "e2f7b0c6-34b9-5cdd-a2c3-dccbfbacb488" :question/math-academy-id "q-127073" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-13}{-7}=\\frac{y+2}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-13}{-7}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{5},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(13,-2,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-7,3,5⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=13-7t \\\\ y=-2+3t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-10bab257-9e49-5588-bdbd-e51321b62eff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-10bab257-9e49-5588-bdbd-e51321b62eff" :answer-field/id #uuid "10bab257-9e49-5588-bdbd-e51321b62eff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5e9eb55-76d8-5834-b077-9d8e4ba666d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8d95702-203e-5dd9-8f89-b3e9ad2f7948" "answer-089f0314-d541-57da-8474-803ac5e9d9f4" "answer-d117c2e1-a8ab-51ed-866a-b2f0126b6bb6" "answer-a5e9eb55-76d8-5834-b077-9d8e4ba666d7" "answer-4c141cec-318c-5fa6-984e-d5d96ba7c25e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8d95702-203e-5dd9-8f89-b3e9ad2f7948" :answer/id #uuid "a8d95702-203e-5dd9-8f89-b3e9ad2f7948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=11+7t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=1+t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-089f0314-d541-57da-8474-803ac5e9d9f4" :answer/id #uuid "089f0314-d541-57da-8474-803ac5e9d9f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=13+7t \\\\ y=-3+2t \\\\ z=1-5t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d117c2e1-a8ab-51ed-866a-b2f0126b6bb6" :answer/id #uuid "d117c2e1-a8ab-51ed-866a-b2f0126b6bb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=13+7t \\\\ y=2+3t \\\\ z=1-5t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5e9eb55-76d8-5834-b077-9d8e4ba666d7" :answer/id #uuid "a5e9eb55-76d8-5834-b077-9d8e4ba666d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=13-7t \\\\ y=-2+3t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c141cec-318c-5fa6-984e-d5d96ba7c25e" :answer/id #uuid "4c141cec-318c-5fa6-984e-d5d96ba7c25e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cf27c214-ec1e-55e8-948b-06e561f6f7e7" :question/id #uuid "cf27c214-ec1e-55e8-948b-06e561f6f7e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-33246" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-3+6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-4t \\\\ 5+2t \\\\ -3+6t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4t \\\\ 2t \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(3,5,-3)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-4}=\\frac{y-5}{2}=\\frac{z-(-3)}{6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-4}=\\frac{y-5}{2}=\\frac{z+3}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6b270efb-9c32-5f2a-a9f0-0cab10121392"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6b270efb-9c32-5f2a-a9f0-0cab10121392" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b270efb-9c32-5f2a-a9f0-0cab10121392" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c2d99a9-ddfb-5a97-abd4-e05bcb1d544a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2000bfc-3f8b-500c-ac25-9de30657d477" "answer-d9ee8d2d-95e8-52c8-884c-18433cf351d2" "answer-1c2d99a9-ddfb-5a97-abd4-e05bcb1d544a" "answer-781dc19c-aaeb-55b8-b85e-398e8c40ddf0" "answer-6e085e60-92ea-59c0-9469-2c2512ee9670"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2000bfc-3f8b-500c-ac25-9de30657d477" :answer/id #uuid "c2000bfc-3f8b-500c-ac25-9de30657d477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{-4}=\\frac{y+5}{2}=\\frac{z+3}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9ee8d2d-95e8-52c8-884c-18433cf351d2" :answer/id #uuid "d9ee8d2d-95e8-52c8-884c-18433cf351d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-6}{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c2d99a9-ddfb-5a97-abd4-e05bcb1d544a" :answer/id #uuid "1c2d99a9-ddfb-5a97-abd4-e05bcb1d544a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{-4}=\\frac{y-5}{2}=\\frac{z+3}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-781dc19c-aaeb-55b8-b85e-398e8c40ddf0" :answer/id #uuid "781dc19c-aaeb-55b8-b85e-398e8c40ddf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-4}{3}=\\frac{y+2}{5}=\\frac{z+6}{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e085e60-92ea-59c0-9469-2c2512ee9670" :answer/id #uuid "6e085e60-92ea-59c0-9469-2c2512ee9670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-4}=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120221 :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the vector equation\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(0,-5,5)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨6,1,-6⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{6}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{1}=\\frac{z-5}{-6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{y+5}{1}=\\frac{z-5}{-6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13a206c5-c050-5343-8992-9fa4de1720b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13a206c5-c050-5343-8992-9fa4de1720b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "13a206c5-c050-5343-8992-9fa4de1720b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f81bd765-d473-5593-847e-f0fd78d42b13" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f81bd765-d473-5593-847e-f0fd78d42b13" "answer-e90875fe-b897-5ee2-a9d0-62239b411734" "answer-59f75482-4344-5455-9326-2b02a2664200" "answer-bab03ceb-16b2-5883-b741-7e3fa8ad18e3" "answer-6c5f12f8-0cc6-5f24-912e-0e0046f905d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f81bd765-d473-5593-847e-f0fd78d42b13" :answer/id #uuid "f81bd765-d473-5593-847e-f0fd78d42b13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{y+5}{1}=\\frac{z-5}{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e90875fe-b897-5ee2-a9d0-62239b411734" :answer/id #uuid "e90875fe-b897-5ee2-a9d0-62239b411734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{y}{1}=\\frac{z}{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59f75482-4344-5455-9326-2b02a2664200" :answer/id #uuid "59f75482-4344-5455-9326-2b02a2664200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+1}{-5}=\\frac{z-6}{5},\\,x=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bab03ceb-16b2-5883-b741-7e3fa8ad18e3" :answer/id #uuid "bab03ceb-16b2-5883-b741-7e3fa8ad18e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-1}{-5}=\\frac{z+6}{5},\\,x=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c5f12f8-0cc6-5f24-912e-0e0046f905d1" :answer/id #uuid "6c5f12f8-0cc6-5f24-912e-0e0046f905d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f4d4cbd-f2d7-5e35-a92b-2f2fb49fe824" :question/id #uuid "2f4d4cbd-f2d7-5e35-a92b-2f2fb49fe824" :question/math-academy-id "q-71037" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{4}=\\frac{y-(-3)}{0}=\\frac{z-4}{1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}=\\frac{y+3}{0}=z-4,\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y+3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=-3:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4+t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y+3}{0}$ part and instead write $y=-3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{4}=z-4,\\,y=-3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02ce321d-f42c-5876-8f33-0ad24f21e148"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02ce321d-f42c-5876-8f33-0ad24f21e148" :answer-field/id #uuid "02ce321d-f42c-5876-8f33-0ad24f21e148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ac0ca21-0772-5ea6-97f1-1ae436ee1c38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2bbe4bc-2ddb-59a9-9664-3eeab65c327b" "answer-fa24ccde-ab5e-541d-abe5-1fc41302c9db" "answer-f7eac140-f9de-54fe-86ec-955c3fb09f92" "answer-0ac0ca21-0772-5ea6-97f1-1ae436ee1c38" "answer-44b3c7a8-f3fd-53ad-a5d7-8900d29452ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2bbe4bc-2ddb-59a9-9664-3eeab65c327b" :answer/id #uuid "a2bbe4bc-2ddb-59a9-9664-3eeab65c327b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=y+3,\\,z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa24ccde-ab5e-541d-abe5-1fc41302c9db" :answer/id #uuid "fa24ccde-ab5e-541d-abe5-1fc41302c9db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=y+3=z-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7eac140-f9de-54fe-86ec-955c3fb09f92" :answer/id #uuid "f7eac140-f9de-54fe-86ec-955c3fb09f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=z+4,\\,y=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ac0ca21-0772-5ea6-97f1-1ae436ee1c38" :answer/id #uuid "0ac0ca21-0772-5ea6-97f1-1ae436ee1c38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=z-4,\\,y=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44b3c7a8-f3fd-53ad-a5d7-8900d29452ba" :answer/id #uuid "44b3c7a8-f3fd-53ad-a5d7-8900d29452ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+3=z-4,\\,x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dbddc051-609a-50f8-b7fd-7c6e4c6d692b" :question/id #uuid "dbddc051-609a-50f8-b7fd-7c6e4c6d692b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127459" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{0}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{1}=\\frac{z-0}{-5}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{0}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z}{-5},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x-7}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=7:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2+t \\\\ -5t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x-7}{0}$ part and instead write $x=7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z}{-5},\\,x=7\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b5ed977-dd6d-5306-bb26-25955c268564"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b5ed977-dd6d-5306-bb26-25955c268564" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5ed977-dd6d-5306-bb26-25955c268564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a040e97c-8a79-5509-87c0-8255b799a192" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b014a37f-26e2-5e8b-b252-a864ef58a225" "answer-91610606-a3e0-593c-bcc2-39d39446b5f2" "answer-a040e97c-8a79-5509-87c0-8255b799a192" "answer-c3db7411-e481-5335-9ae6-c020ef03327f" "answer-af79ec3c-58c8-52c7-bd5a-209a42167d84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b014a37f-26e2-5e8b-b252-a864ef58a225" :answer/id #uuid "b014a37f-26e2-5e8b-b252-a864ef58a225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+1}{2}=\\frac{z}{5},\\,x=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91610606-a3e0-593c-bcc2-39d39446b5f2" :answer/id #uuid "91610606-a3e0-593c-bcc2-39d39446b5f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{-5}=\\frac{z}{1},\\,x=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a040e97c-8a79-5509-87c0-8255b799a192" :answer/id #uuid "a040e97c-8a79-5509-87c0-8255b799a192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z}{-5},\\,x=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3db7411-e481-5335-9ae6-c020ef03327f" :answer/id #uuid "c3db7411-e481-5335-9ae6-c020ef03327f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{1}=\\frac{z}{-5},\\,x=-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af79ec3c-58c8-52c7-bd5a-209a42167d84" :answer/id #uuid "af79ec3c-58c8-52c7-bd5a-209a42167d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{1}=\\frac{z}{5},\\,x=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e1761a52-f68d-5dfd-83a7-02fd5760a09e" :question/id #uuid "e1761a52-f68d-5dfd-83a7-02fd5760a09e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127460" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-(-6)}{5}=\\frac{z-13}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y+6}{5}=\\frac{z-13}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z-13}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=13:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1-2t \\\\ -6+5t \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-13}{0}$ part and instead write $z=13$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y+6}{5},\\,z=13\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8dace27d-7465-57cd-b6cc-1a69b60f0f81"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8dace27d-7465-57cd-b6cc-1a69b60f0f81" :answer-field/id #uuid "8dace27d-7465-57cd-b6cc-1a69b60f0f81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5633467-6d30-59cb-a103-1df0f479fc35" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13aa6270-4f47-57d9-96d5-e04d9559c1dd" "answer-ebf8ec86-3cc9-58ca-b77d-738394e52afc" "answer-b5633467-6d30-59cb-a103-1df0f479fc35" "answer-03a0481f-9850-51a2-93a8-9cb1375be70e" "answer-5147f586-12cc-5846-9c2a-91a6e6aae45a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13aa6270-4f47-57d9-96d5-e04d9559c1dd" :answer/id #uuid "13aa6270-4f47-57d9-96d5-e04d9559c1dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{2}=\\frac{y+6}{5},\\,z=-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebf8ec86-3cc9-58ca-b77d-738394e52afc" :answer/id #uuid "ebf8ec86-3cc9-58ca-b77d-738394e52afc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y+5}{6},\\,z=-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5633467-6d30-59cb-a103-1df0f479fc35" :answer/id #uuid "b5633467-6d30-59cb-a103-1df0f479fc35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y+6}{5},\\,z=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03a0481f-9850-51a2-93a8-9cb1375be70e" :answer/id #uuid "03a0481f-9850-51a2-93a8-9cb1375be70e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{-5}=\\frac{y+6}{2},\\,z=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5147f586-12cc-5846-9c2a-91a6e6aae45a" :answer/id #uuid "5147f586-12cc-5846-9c2a-91a6e6aae45a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{-1}=\\frac{y+6}{5},\\,z=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-999b5494-410f-5564-a5e2-d9dbe0ae34c9" :question/id #uuid "999b5494-410f-5564-a5e2-d9dbe0ae34c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127464" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(7,-1,0)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,1,-4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{1}=\\frac{z-0}{-4}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z}{-4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c9478fb-99b4-566d-b0ee-d81368042926"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c9478fb-99b4-566d-b0ee-d81368042926" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9478fb-99b4-566d-b0ee-d81368042926" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b23463d1-7983-5832-a155-38676beb3e86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83bd26ba-9b94-5213-87dd-4f816b559e83" "answer-6f85a2de-8936-53e9-b4c3-0d80c357fcab" "answer-b23463d1-7983-5832-a155-38676beb3e86" "answer-e7220639-4d6c-573b-b6b7-5fc1ded2cead" "answer-e3b20a42-f8fc-5421-82ef-f6666475bd47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83bd26ba-9b94-5213-87dd-4f816b559e83" :answer/id #uuid "83bd26ba-9b94-5213-87dd-4f816b559e83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{-3}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f85a2de-8936-53e9-b4c3-0d80c357fcab" :answer/id #uuid "6f85a2de-8936-53e9-b4c3-0d80c357fcab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{-3}=\\frac{y-1}{1}=\\frac{z}{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b23463d1-7983-5832-a155-38676beb3e86" :answer/id #uuid "b23463d1-7983-5832-a155-38676beb3e86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z}{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7220639-4d6c-573b-b6b7-5fc1ded2cead" :answer/id #uuid "e7220639-4d6c-573b-b6b7-5fc1ded2cead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3b20a42-f8fc-5421-82ef-f6666475bd47" :answer/id #uuid "e3b20a42-f8fc-5421-82ef-f6666475bd47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y+1}{4}=\\frac{z}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121048 :tutorial/content "Suppose we know that the vector equation of the line $l$ is given by\n![](images/92/92c5ed55727717320b9c128adf1a6d786666adb38cd6ba71d57917e60d661fd8.svg)\n\nand we want to rewrite it using Cartesian coordinates. In other words, we want to create an equation that relates $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ to each other.\n\nWe can do this using the following $3$ steps.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the parametric equations for the line.\n\nSubstituting ![](images/67/67b8360f90540ffb75d39717c375f0ef6e9a8a39cae5832c78957105e0d148b6.svg) into the equation of $l,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3+6t \\\\ -2+5t \\\\ 5-t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3+6t \\\\ y=-2+5t \\\\ z=5-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Solve for $t$ in each of the parametric equations.\n\n![](images/ee/eed0a210b121af73bc2ceab04b95def59239a742055284e706a1532b47edc60d.svg)\n\n**Step 3:** Equate the resulting expressions. Because the right-hand side of each equation is equal to $t,$ we can write this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-3}{6}=\\dfrac{y+2}{5}=\\dfrac{z-5}{-1} = t\n$$\n\nWe can simplify further by omitting the \"$=t$\" on the right-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-3}{6}=\\dfrac{y+2}{5}=\\dfrac{z-5}{-1} \\,.\n$$\n\nAnd we are done! \n\nThis way of writing the equation of a line is called the **Cartesian equation** or **Cartesian canonical equation** (or simply **canonical equation**).\n\nIn general, the Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is parallel to the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle v_x, v_y, v_z \\rangle$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-x_0}{v_x}=\\dfrac{y-y_0}{v_y}=\\dfrac{z-z_0}{v_z} = t, \\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121055 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to write the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n![](images/9d/9d4a6d56170de2e0dbfa7e2a6f51905b19f9ada9fa1900aafe2672f54831be86.svg)\n\nUsing the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{5}=\\dfrac{z-3}{0} = t,\t\\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty),\n$$\n\nor equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{5}=\\dfrac{z-3}{0}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\dfrac{z-3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/0b/0bea89e098af6be643450df08d30b97c0c3d658075b0b891ab2c4c7f37077f42.svg)\n\nIf we solve for $t$ in the parametric equations of the line, we get\n\n![](images/f3/f399dae55ae8c720f7769fa78a42b30b2a7b7aab49ed1515d9c43d371f3a9f71.svg)\n\nOnly the first two equations have right-hand sides equal to $t,$ so we combine them but keep the third equation separate:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{5}, \\; z=3\n$$\n\nSo, it's as if we removed the $\\dfrac{z-3}{0}$ part in the original formula and replaced it with $z=3.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120015 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
